{
  "dom_id": "step-q97161",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Given that $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.1),$ compute $P(4<X\\le 10)$ rounded to $4$ decimal places.",
  "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.1),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(0.9)}^{x-1}(0.1), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4<X\\le 10) & =P(X\\in \\{5,6,7,8,9,10\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=5)+P(X=6)+P(X=7)+ \\\\  & \\,P(X=8)+P(X=9)+P(X=10) \\\\  & =f(5)+f(6)+f(7)+f(8)+f(9)+f(10) \\\\  & ={(0.9)}^{4}(0.1)+{(0.9)}^{5}(0.1)+{(0.9)}^{6}(0.1)+ \\\\  & \\,{(0.9)}^{7}(0.1)+{(0.9)}^{8}(0.1)+{(0.9)}^{9}(0.1) \\\\  & ≈0.3074.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
